      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5ac4fd763f8d523278a414f7|full_name}: That's also a good idea.\nMain reason I'm sort of hoping for something like this is so we can make worlds where those of us that just need to talk to someone at some point without a lot of other people listening in on the conversation.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-09-17T17:54:50.656Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Either for the SDK itself on new worlds or in general.\nThe thought is that it's very disorientating to hear conversations going on in other rooms or on other floors.\nWhat I'm thinking is something along the lines of when a connected VRChat client gets a VoIP packet or a audio trigger from another client (I don't know VRChat's client<->server<->client topology), the receiving client does a ray-cast test in the direction of the \"sender\" of the audio to determine if there is in fact a wall or ceiling between them.\nI'm thinking some form of collision test on a trajectory pointed toward the sender client as an example.\n\nThis could also probably make it possible for someone that want's to have a private conversation to not be overheard.",
